  "instance_name": "muhammad_perfect",
  "label": "Reference to Muhammad as 'Perfect' or 'The Perfect Example'",
  "description": "This is a core concept in Islam, where Muhammad is considered the final prophet and the perfect example (Al-As-Saadiq Al-Amin) for Muslims to follow. The meme uses this reference to imply that if Muhammad endorsed camel urine as medicine, then it must be true or acceptable, thereby attempting to validate the claim. This is a misrepresentation of Islamic theology, as the context of hadiths is often nuanced and not meant to be taken literally or as a blanket endorsement of all practices.",
